{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles","id":88863,"title":"\"Twitch Plays Pokemon\" and other Solar Circles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-11T08:48:53-07:00","id":88863,"title":"\"Twitch Plays Pokemon\" and other Solar Circles","content":"One thing I've often been challenged by on Exalted's basic premise is thinking of examples of circles, rather than just individual Exalted. A lot of our references- Hercules, Arjuna, etc. tend to be fairly independent.<br /> <br /> Then I realized that you could probably pitch the Israelite leaders in Exodus as a party of Solars; Moses is the Zenith, Aaron is the Eclipse, Joshua is the Dawn- you can even work Miriam as a Night caste.<br /> <br /> From this it also occurred to me that you could distribute Solar Exaltations to Mohammed and his followers; to Justinian and Belisarius.<br /> <br /> I'd be lying if I didn't say the cognitive spark of looking for groups where the key players display a mixture of religious authority, charisma, and willingness to use force (with the weight of each trait varying from individual to individual) did not come from this poster, no doubt distributed by the local chapter of the Wyld Hunt: <a href=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Bib9mWICYAA1b76.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Bib9mWICYAA1b76.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Edit: Can you think of any other examples that have been useful for you in conceptualizing stories where the Circle works as a team, rather than 2-5 powerful people that all know each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","user":"GhostTurtle","date":".  Edited to be less cryptic. 03-11-2014, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T09:13:50-07:00","id":88870,"title":"","content":"Not quite sure as to what the purpose of the thread is, but there are definitely groups of heroes in history - argonauts, knights of the round table, three bogatyrs, the brotherhood of the ring, the avengers, etc.<br /> <br /> The reason we always think about Exalted in terms of circles is because Exalted (gasp) is a group gaming activity. You definitely can have solo adventures, but the basic premise of the RPGs is that you are playing with friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T12:28:46-07:00","id":88988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles?p=88870#post88870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite sure as to what the purpose of the thread is, but there are definitely groups of heroes in history - argonauts, knights of the round table, three bogatyrs, the brotherhood of the ring, the avengers, etc.<br /> <br /> The reason we always think about Exalted in terms of circles is because Exalted (gasp) is a group gaming activity. You definitely can have solo adventures, but the basic premise of the RPGs is that you are playing with friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure part of the reason is that, well, a lot of the usual inspirations are... not exactly team people. It can give something of a wrong impression and end up with Exalted campaigns being more about five separate stories that are forced together by awkward social contract and less about the story of a group, if pretty much all the examples people give out are generally of people who were worse at team play than the Decepticons!<br /> <br /> :P<br /> <br /> (The &quot;epic motivation&quot; thing also has historically not helped on this stuff, while we're on this. When the book insists that Exalts are phenomenally driven people, and that you have to pick an all-encompassing drive that you want above all other things to accomplish, and then <i>every character in the circle has a completely different motivation</i>, well. There can sometimes be a certain feeling of &quot;why are we even staying together, again?&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 03-11-2014, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T14:38:26-07:00","id":89052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles?p=88870#post88870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite sure as to what the purpose of the thread is</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sorry, I guess I should have been a bit more clear on what I was going for here-I've edited the OP accordingly. Really I'm curious about exactly what Dracsin mentions: examples of stories where the protagonists are plausible inspirations for Solars, and actually work together on a regular basis towards a common goal, rather than occasionally meeting up to stop some existential threat that overwhelms whatever personal narrative they have. Basically, teams where they're all on-screen most of the time, rather than just the final boss-fight.<br /> <br /> For example, I don't really understand the Avengers or the Justice League, at least from my limited experience of them, as being useful examples of the sort of stories you'd tell about a Solar Circle. Most of the time, Ironman, the Hulk, and Thor are all pursuing their own very different adventures; it's only when some alien super-fleet shows up that they all converge onto one battlefield.<br /> <br /> The party from Twitch Plays Pokemon is a Solar Circle because their individual legends within the community are thoroughly intertwined, and are all thought of as working together to serve Lord Helix/beat the game/whatever. Each gets their turn to shine, but they're all traveling together all the time, and working towards the same goal.<br /> <br /> The party from Exodus is a Solar Circle because, again, they work together towards the same goal. They spend a considerable portion of their time on-screen together, either discussing their next step in leading the other Israelites or directly suppporting one another, as Moses channels divine inspiration into Aaron, who gives a rousing speech to the fighters that Joshua leads into battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T15:04:41-07:00","id":89064,"title":"","content":"This thread makes me want to run the Star Sheriffs as a Sidereal Circle...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T15:38:17-07:00","id":89073,"title":"","content":"Brotherhood of the Ring.<br /> Mighty Morphing Power Rangers.<br /> Kyle, Stan, Cartman and Kenny.<br /> Knights of the Round Table.<br /> Alucard, Seras and Integra.<br /> Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.<br /> Samurai Pizza Cats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 03-11-2014, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T15:59:47-07:00","id":89079,"title":"","content":"These might not be the best examples.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles?p=89073#post89073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brotherhood of the Ring.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were all doing their own thing before Sauron reared his ugly head, and split up less than a third of a way through their chronicle.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mighty Morphing Power Rangers. </div> </div> </div>Best buds when not on the job, but they're still facing a world-shattering threat... supposedly.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kyle, Stan, Cartman and Kenny. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what keeps those kids together. At the very least, they should have stopped inviting Cartman.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Knights of the Round Table. </div> </div> </div>Those guys didn't really team up on anything, ever. Even with the Grail Hunt, in which all the knights participated, everyone went their own way. The rest of the time, it seems like they were just drinking buddies in Camelot when they weren't running off on their own quests.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles. </div> </div> </div>Bound together by circumstance - namely, being raised as brothers and being unable to live among humans because they're giant freaking turtles.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, though, I'm at a loss for good examples. The only ones I can really come up with are various Bioware RPG dudes (the Baalspawn, Hawke, the Exile), who gather up a bunch of capable heroes by doing them favors and then keep them together mostly by force of personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 03-11-2014, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T17:17:27-07:00","id":89128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles?p=89052#post89052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, I don't really understand the Avengers or the Justice League, at least from my limited experience of them, as being useful examples of the sort of stories you'd tell about a Solar Circle. Most of the time, Ironman, the Hulk, and Thor are all pursuing their own very different adventures; it's only when some alien super-fleet shows up that they all converge onto one battlefield.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the fact that those guys have individual adventures impeaches the teamwork they display when brought together. There isn't a rule that a circle has to work together all the time, other than the simple rule that it is easier to have the circle work together because that's easier in the rpg medium.<br /> <br /> Which contrast with the medium of comics where there's an economic interest in expanding on individual stories. In comics, the medium pushes towards both team and individual books at the same time,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles?p=89079#post89079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, though, I'm at a loss for good examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about Rama, Lakshmana, &amp; Hanuman and Jason &amp; the Argonauts? King Mob &amp; the Invisibles? Swamp Thing, John Constantine, Deadman, Etrigan , and the Phantom Stranger when they all fight Hell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":1338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","user":"BvBPL","date":". 03-11-2014, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T18:23:30-07:00","id":89156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles?p=89128#post89128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that the fact that those guys have individual adventures impeaches the teamwork they display when brought together. There isn't a rule that a circle has to work together all the time, other than the simple rule that it is easier to have the circle work together because that's easier in the rpg medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me clarify further: I don't mean to denigrate the Avengers, etc. as not having real teamwork. What I'm saying is that I don't find them very useful as a guide for how to run an Exalted campaign where you have players who have to sit through any scenes where their character isn't present. I find it hard enough to get people to commit for 3 hours of game without then telling them they only get to play their character for a small portion of that time.<br /> <br /> Exalted is competing with D&amp;D, yeah? In D&amp;D, the default narrative is one of a bunch of hired thugs sent to loot and pillage some monster-infested ruin. Say what you will about the weakness of that narrative, at least all 4 thugs pursue their interest in killing green people and taking their gold <i>together.</i> They work together as an adventuring company. The fighter and the rogue may have their own subplots which occasionally come up, but most of the time the rogue is picking locks so the fighter can run through the door and stab things.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for examples of Solar Circles that operate chiefly as a team in other media as an exercise in coming up with campaigns that are about heroes of arete empowered by the gods who also happen to work as a team most of the time. The Avengers are limited in this instance because their plots, at least as I have experienced them, are &quot;there is some bad guy so bad that we need to drop our own storylines and team up to fight her/him/it/them together!&quot; Sure, they work together to deal with this, but I'm not sure I can make every session of Exalted an existential boss fight.<br /> <br /> So far, the best examples I've found are religious/revolutionary groups. This way the Dawn can lead the troops, the Zenith can inspire the faithful, the Night can guard against internal threats, the Twilight can build cool stuff/heal the injured, and the Eclipse can handle any negotiations. I've yet to run this, but it seems like game-play would consist of the PCs spending a lot of time in the command tent, meeting with external rulers, handling complaints brought by their lieutenants, and discussing how to deal with particular problems.<br /> <br /> The way the Solars have generally been presented previously is as a bunch of exceptional individuals who Exalt and then happen to run into each other, and occasionally find reason to work together. This makes for great chapter fiction, but if you want to run a campaign about 4 of them, it would seem that you need to make their stories overlap a lot more than that.<br /> <br /> As another example, I suspect you could have the Solars all be in the ruling cabinet of a kingdom. You could possibly get away with them being Robert Baratheon (Dawn), Eddard Stark (Zenith), Varys (Night), Petyr Baelish (Eclipse), and Grand Maester Pycelle (Twilight).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","user":"GhostTurtle","date":". 03-11-2014, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T18:34:23-07:00","id":89159,"title":"","content":"Errr, the legendary Lord Helix the Zenith who was resurrected from a Dragon King Stasis Chamber and his crusader companion Bird Jesus? Together, they traveled to Autochthon's Elemental Pole of Lightning to tame the Lightning Elemental Hero AJ who came back to Creation with them to battle the Defiler False Prophet who hijacked I AM to delete up and coming heroes from the Loom before they realize their true potential.<br /> <br /> Many trees stood in their way. Misty was defeated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T20:04:26-07:00","id":89196,"title":"","content":"~~<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles?p=89156#post89156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it hard enough to get people to commit for 3 hours of game without then telling them they only get to play their character for a small portion of that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>As something of an aside, I think the current rules 2e rules system forces players to sit on their hands during many activities. Dawns take up a disproportionate amount of time during combat whereas Eclipses take up a lot during social encounters.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exalted is competing with D&amp;D, yeah? In D&amp;D, the default narrative is one of a bunch of hired thugs sent to loot and pillage some monster-infested ruin. Say what you will about the weakness of that narrative, at least all 4 thugs pursue their interest in killing green people and taking their gold <i>together.</i> They work together as an adventuring company. The fighter and the rogue may have their own subplots which occasionally come up, but most of the time the rogue is picking locks so the fighter can run through the door and stab things. </div> </div> </div>That's in large part because the rpg medium is set up, as a default, to maximize entertainment as a group endeavor. It is possible to run games that use different social interactions to introduce different means of entertainment, but those systems require something beyond the base level of competency of players and GMs. That it is generally best to not split the party doesn't mean it is always best.<br /> I'm not point that out to impeach you or disagree with you, but rather to add a broader perspective. Generally, I would rather play or run a game that keeps the party together, but I don't foreclose upon the option that a well run game with competent players couldn't have fun splitting up the party.<br /> You can contrast the system of don't split up the party to maximize entertainment with the comic medium. In rpgs, everyone's time is generally limited and important meaning that it is generally better to work together as a team. However, the Avengers' time isn't so limited. Iron Man can fly off to space to fight space aliens and still be back in time to fight with the Avengers because the time restrictions that players face do not apply to Iron Man. Plus Iron Man is going to be in a lot more comics than any single game group will ever have sessions so there\u2019s going to be more variance for presentation.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So far, the best examples I've found are religious/revolutionary groups. </div> </div> </div> I\u2019d say Grant Morrison\u2019s The Invisibles is right up your alley as a model. The Iliad would be another good choice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026if you want to run a campaign about 4 of them, it would seem that you need to make their stories overlap a lot more than that. </div> </div> </div>I think most ensemble fiction that has a continuing relationship starts that relationship via happenstance and then continues because a shared goal or values or whatever consequently develops. Exalted is interesting though because there's the aspect of the Second Breath. It would be interesting to see the characters start as mortals who are subsequently exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":1338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","user":"BvBPL","date":". 03-11-2014, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T22:16:11-07:00","id":89264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles#post88863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've often been challenged by on Exalted's basic premise is thinking of examples of circles, rather than just individual Exalted. A lot of our references- Hercules, Arjuna, etc. tend to be fairly independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm? What with the other Pandavas, I think he's a perfect example of either a Solar in a circle. Or a DB in a sworn (and in this case literal) brotherhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","name":"SurlySeraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T08:01:37-07:00","id":89484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SurlySeraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/88863-twitch-plays-pokemon-and-other-solar-circles?p=89264#post89264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm? What with the other Pandavas, I think he's a perfect example of either a Solar in a circle. Or a DB in a sworn (and in this case literal) brotherhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly my experience with Arjuna is mostly the Bhagavad Ghita, where he comes across as a lone Dawn talked down from a Limit Break by his Sidereal charioteer. Looking at the adventures of him and his brothers, you're right-there is a stronger Circle-esque dynamic there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T00:37:43-07:00","id":90015,"title":"","content":"Okay, it looks like y'all need some ENSEMBLE CAST input. So. Here we go.<br /> <br /> <b>The Party of Two:</b><br /> If you don't know it, check out Fafhrd and the Gray Mouser: They star in a number of sword-and-sorcery stories from back in the good old days when fantasy was pulpy and sword and sorcery was less Tolkien and more Burroughs and Moorcock. Fafhrd was the mighty Dawn caste warrior, and the Gray Mouser was a Night caste of incredible sophistaction. They were bros before people started using the word bros, and got each other into and out of all manner of difficulties, sometimes involving treasure and sometimes involving romance and often involving a bit of comedy. Two players is the smallest I'm willing to go when I run a game, because parties of one are boring, so I'll start with these guys.<br /> <br /> For additional party-of-two dynamic ideas, try Sherlock and Watson (badass Watson, not incompetent Watson or sexy Watson or gay Watson-there are many Watsons) for a Twilight and a Dawn caste doctor (now that's a great character concept right there!). You can also go Gilgamesh and Enkidu, and if your players are comfortable with it you can add a little romance to the mix you can get all manner of delightful interpersonal complications. If you're looking for a reason for a party of two to stick together even though they have severely different life goals, make 'em family: siblings, parent-and-kid, lovers, or even a married couple. This trick also works to keep sections of a larger party together.<br /> <br /> <b>The Party of Three: </b><br /> Here, you'll want to look no farther than Buffy, because if there's anything Joss Whedon does well, it's ensemble casts. Buffy is a great dawn, and her party members start out as mortals (though Giles the Sidereal helps get them all on the path to hero town) but Willow turns into a badass Twilight. Xander stays a heroic mortal the whole time, showcasing many of the really fun and interesting party dynamics you can have if your players are willing to play at different power levels: his desire to be useful to the team and his insecurity about his abilities to do so drive a lot of interest plot for the whole party. Other players join the group occasionally and showcase all manner of useful dynamics: interparty romance, interparty betrayals of trust or confidence, interventions over addictive behavior, etc. Lots of social dynamic ideas here. Notable Exalted inspiration in the show includes Faith and Angel and Spike as Abyssals (and hell, Drusilla too), a fourth-season casting of Unity of the Closed Fist, everything the Watchers do as Sidereal fodder, and the emotional and interpersonal consequences of power and regularly fighting off apocalypses.<br /> <br /> Also, Kirk and Spock and McCoy are the best trio. Just...the best.<br /> <br /> For additional party of three ideas, take a look at the Power Trio page over on TV Tropes for a number of common party dynamics. In fact, check out the Four Man Band, Five Man Band, and Battle Couple and Adventure Couple pages as well. If you're looking to create a stable party with interesting dynamics, those pages are a gold mine.<br /> <br /> <b>Party of Four:</b> Here you'll want to take a look at Avatar: The Last Airbender, in particular the second and third seasons. The main characters are all Exalted whose raw power level makes them Solars in comparison to the world around them and their ability to change it by sheer force, so don't get hung up on their elemental affinities. Sokka's actually a Sidereal Half-Caste, by the way. You'll note that once it becomes a party of five, they start splitting into smaller groups to do things on their own. This is because four is most you can count up to instinctively (a lot of magic tricks and misdirection rely on that fact, by the way): once there are five people it starts getting harder for the audience to track them.<br /> <br /> <b>Party of Five:</b> This is the largest number of PCs I generally like to run. It means each PC only has to keep track of four other PCs, which is generally the largest number of PCs they can be relied upon to become emotionally invested in: larger groups tend to sort themselves into smaller clumps or cliques, and the point at which it gets harder to give everyone screen time to develop their own personal plots. Generally once the party is this large you have to focus them on a unified goal or they start breaking up. You can find good examples of parties of Five or higher in more Whedon-works (Firefly is great Exalted inspiration particularly if you're running Heaven's Reach: the party has a Zenith, his Full Moon mate, a Dawn, a Twilight, an Air Aspect, a Chosen of Serenity, an Eclipse, a Chosen of Secrets, and an Abyssal). It's hard to keep a party this big stable, and the best way to do it is by having each player have some manner of unbreakable bond to at least two other players.<br /> <br /> Now, I know you're looking for &quot;party of Solars&quot; here, rather than mixed parties. But here's the thing: ANY character, from ANY of these pieces of source material, could be a Solar. Solars are humans who can change the world due to unsurpassed skill. Kirk doesn't need to be able to glow or summon demons or shoot fire out his ass: he is a leader, and he's brilliant Zenith or Dawn, or hell even Eclipse inspiration for your characters. Look not to their powerset, for they're in a different universe: look to their role in the story. Are they an explorer, a negotiator, a leader, a scholar? These archetypes are what castes are built on, and anyone badass enough to be an impressive Main Character is probably worthy Solar inspiration.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T01:57:06-07:00","id":90053,"title":"","content":"Mostly what Wise Old Guru said, but some additional thoughts:<br /> <br /> If you want to keep the cast together most of the time, it'll be hard to find inspiration if there are more than three or so characters. But then, as far as my own gaming experience goes... you will <i>never</i> succeed in keeping the party together all the time. It just won't happen. But, if you're satisfied with <i>most</i> of the time (which is really all you'll generally get), there are a bunch of examples - basically anything with an ensemble cast. Wise Old Guru threw out Firefly, which is a good example, but some others do come to mind. So here, I'll just toss out a bunch of examples at various party sizes (mostly anime, because it's the medium I happen to have substantial lists of at my disposal, and I've been watching a bunch lately):<br /> <br /> Two to Three<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Castle<br /> Elementary<br /> Sherlock<br /> El Cazador de la Bruja<br /> Precure Series (numerous - Futari wa, Max Heart, Splash Star, Suite, a lot of Heartcatch and Fresh)<br /> Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha, Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha A's<br /> Senki Zesshou Symphogear<br /> Mai-HiME<br /> Ga-Rei-Zero (depending on how you slice it)<br /> Buddy Complex<br /> Log Horizon (at least what I've seen)<br /> Supernatural<br /> Sabriel (all three, really)<br /> Powers<br /> Lord of the Rings, post-Breaking (really, post-Fellowship the story is three of these - if you have eight players who want to play, this would be a hell of a way to kick off several separate games)<br /> Original Shannara trilogy</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Four or more<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (while there are individual flashback episodes, there is a very solid core cast that shows up most of the time, even if it fluctuates a bit)<br /> Wakfu<br /> Young Justice<br /> Lord of the Rings, pre-Breaking<br /> Every Power Rangers, ever<br /> Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS (which set of four are the PCs is open to interpretation)<br /> Precure Series (Splash Star, Smile, Yes!, parts of Fresh and Heartcatch)<br /> Puella Magi Madoka Magica (albeit with a group of players with very different interests than a party of Exalted players usually will)<br /> Genei wo Kakeru Taiyou<br /> David Eddings' Belgariad, Mallorean, Elenium, and Tamuli, as well as the Redemption of Althalus (kind of)<br /> Gundam 00</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Note that all of these examples fit into at least one of three categories:<br /> Bound together by holding the same job or calling<br /> Bound together by a quest<br /> Bound together by circumstances beyond their control<br /> <br /> It is <i>possible</i> to do other combined plot types with a coherent group, but it's <i>hard</i>. Since the third plot type doesn't work extraordinarily well with Exalted, and the first constrains stories pretty thoroughly in the first, you tend to default to quests (whether explicit, standard &quot;destroy the dark lord&quot;, more implicit &quot;keep this town safe&quot;, or more variable &quot;well this one character's plot just came to the front&quot; sort of deals).<br /> <br /> As for how to structure parties, Guru is wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T03:10:08-07:00","id":90073,"title":"","content":"I find that, over long games, party's will get to the point where they stick together even beyond the quest or job or whatever. In the Celestial game I play, which has been going for years, at the beginning we were just a bunch of Celestials who met up, then ran away from the Wyld Hunt together essentially, but now two characters are married, and one of those is my adopted daughter. So eventually you don't need to keep them together as they'll do it themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T01:14:43-07:00","id":91474,"title":"","content":"What, a whole page and no one pointed out that 5 is the traditional number for a boyband?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> and now, taking the stage... DRAGONFORCE! The Terrestrial Music Phenomenon!<br /> <br /> Yeah, i've been thinking about doing that as a game for a few weeks now.<br /> <br /> A sworn brotherhood or 5 terrestrial warrior-poets, on tour around the threshold. Watch them balance performance commitments with random wild hunts and other assorted side-quests. Keep and eye out for that shifty general manager. Is he an anathema in disguise? And above all.... don't let the fans getcha. Those dog-pile grapple rules are mean.<br /> <br /> Rock on. You've got a show in five!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}